From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: do not use a bash redirection

configure runs with /bin/sh, but uses the bash redirection &> to check
for bpftool. A POSIX shell such as dash runs "command -v $BPFTOOL" in
the background instead, so configure replaces BPFTOOL with the output
of whereis and does not find bpftool, although it is available.

Use >/dev/null 2>&1, which all shells support.

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
---
 configure | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -109,11 +109,11 @@
         exit 1
     fi
 
-    if ! command -v $BPFTOOL &>/dev/null; then
+    if ! command -v $BPFTOOL >/dev/null 2>&1; then
         BPFTOOL=$(whereis -b bpftool | awk '{print $2}')
     fi
 
-    if command -v $BPFTOOL &>/dev/null && $BPFTOOL gen help 2>&1 | grep 'gen skeleton.*name' > /dev/null; then
+    if command -v $BPFTOOL >/dev/null 2>&1 && $BPFTOOL gen help 2>&1 | grep 'gen skeleton.*name' > /dev/null; then
         bpftool_version=$($BPFTOOL version | head -n 1)
         echo "using $bpftool_version"
     else
